    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0911" n="899" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg899"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 PW/1–645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-16T16:00:00-04:00">January 16, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. Your telegram 20, January 6, 2 p.m. In instruction no. 19 of July 15, 1944 to
                    our member on War Crimes Commission, London,<anchor n="79" xml:id="d653-f1"/>
                    Department took position that for Commission purposes war in Far East started
                    July 7, 1937. Matter is being called to attention of our deputy member on London
                        Commission<anchor n="80" xml:id="d653-f2"/> who will be in London shortly
                    and who will endeavor to expedite decision by Commission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d653-f1" n="79" xml:id="d653-f1-content">
                <p>Herbert C. Pell; for instruction, see <ref target="frus1944v01#pg_1333">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1944, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 1333</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d653-f2" n="80" xml:id="d653-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Joseph V. Hodgson.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
